      "slug": "cereal-production-is-1-5x-higher-than-in-1972",
      "title": "Cereal Production Climbed 1.5x Since 1972",
      "hook": "The 1970s warned the world would run out of food. The actual numbers went the other direction.",
      "says": [
        "In 1985, progression to secondary school (%) was 77.8. By 2017, it reached 91.3 — 1.2 times higher.",
        "In 1972, cereal production was 1083.7 million metric tons. By 2024, it reached 1644.1 million metric tons — 1.5 times higher.",
        "China leads at 5.2 million square kilometers of farmland, then the United States at 4.2 million, Australia at 3.6 million, Brazil at 2.4 million, and Russia at 2.2 million."
      ],
      "closing": "The famine everyone predicted never arrived. School advanced, grain climbed, and the forecast quietly missed the harvest.",
      "question": "Which number surprised you most — school, grain, or land?"
    },
    {
      "slug": "combustible-renewables-and-waste-is-3-0x-higher-than-in-1990",
      "title": "Waste-Based Energy Grew 3.0x Since 1990",
      "hook": "One energy source has tripled since 1990, and it isn't solar or wind. The answer is what we discard.",
      "says": [
        "In 1990, combustible renewables and waste was 10.2 % of total energy. By 2024, it reached 30.1 % of total energy — 3.0 times higher.",
        "In 1998, access to electricity was 73.2 % of population. By 2024, it reached 91.9 % of population — 1.3 times higher.",
        "In 1972, methane (ch4) emissions from waste was 903.8 Mt CO2e. By 2024, it reached 1,652 Mt CO2e — 1.8 times higher."
      ],
      "closing": "A third of the world's energy now comes from things people once treated as useless.",
      "question": "Which number surprised you most — fuel, power, or waste?"
    },
    {
      "slug": "population-growth-fell-54-since-1972",
      "title": "Population Growth Fell 54% Since 1972",
      "hook": "Population growth was supposed to accelerate forever. Instead, the curve nearly stopped climbing.",
      "says": [
